2. Longest Substring w/o repeating substring:

Code:
class Solution {
    public int lengthOfLongestSubstring(String s) {
        HashSet<Character> set = new HashSet<>();

        int left = 0;
        int maxLength = 0;

        for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {

            // Duplicate found
            while (set.contains(s.charAt(right))) {
                set.remove(s.charAt(left));
                left++;
            }

            // Add current character
            set.add(s.charAt(right));

            // Calculate current window length
            int length = right - left + 1;

            // Update maximum length
            if (length > maxLength) {
                maxLength = length;
            }
        }

        return maxLength;
    }
}

Approach:
Use the sliding window technique with a HashSet to maintain unique characters in the current window. Expand right; when a duplicate is found, move left forward and remove characters until the window contains only unique characters.

Complexity:
Time: O(n) — each character is added and removed from the set at most once.
Space: O(min(n, charset)) — the HashSet stores characters in the current window.

Optimal Code:
class Solution {
    public int lengthOfLongestSubstring(String s) {
        int[] lastIndex = new int[128];
        int left = 0;
        int len = 0;
        for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {
            char ch = s.charAt(right);
            if (lastIndex[ch] > left) {
                left = lastIndex[ch];
            }
            len = Math.max(len, right - left + 1);
            lastIndex[ch] = right + 1;
        }
        return len;
    }
}

Approach:
Use a sliding window with a last-index array to track the most recent position of each character. When a duplicate appears inside the current window, move left directly to the character's next position instead of removing characters one by one.

Complexity:
Time: O(n) — each character is processed once.
Space: O(1) — the array has a fixed size of 128 characters.

